## Why This Is Asked
Understanding end-to-end streaming ingestion, privacy handling, and basic rollback in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming
- Dataflow DoFn masking
- BigQuery per-tenant datasets
- Data Catalog data contracts and lineage
- Quarantine path and 24h rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow DoFn: mask PII before write
class MaskPIIFn {
  process(element) {
    // element is a JSON object
    if (element.email) element.email = maskEmail(element.email);
    if (element.phone) element.phone = maskPhone(element.phone);
    return element;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this pipeline for schema drift and masking correctness?
- How would you alert on quarantine volume spikes and auto-remediate?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design complex, scalable pipelines with dynamic schemas, per-tenant isolation, and robust rollback. Evaluates integration of Pub/Sub, Dataflow, BigQuery, Data Catalog, and access controls, plus testing and lineage practices.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic schema versioning and canonicalization
- Per-tenant access controls (Authorized Views)
- Schema evolution and backfill strategies
- End-to-end data lineage and contracts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo Beam map to canonical schema (high level)
PCollection<Event> events = pubsub.readEvents("projects/.../topics/...");
events.apply(ParDo.of(new DoFn<EncryptedEvent, CanonicalEvent>() {
  @ProcessElement
  public void process(@Element EncryptedEvent e, OutputReceiver<CanonicalEvent> out) {
    CanonicalEvent c = mapToCanonical(e); // uses tenant-specific schema_version
    out.output(c);
  }
}));
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test schema drift without production impact?
- How would you implement data contracts in Data Catalog and enforce them at ingestion?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical data quality, governance, rollback, and per-tenant isolation on GCP, with real components like Pub/Sub, Dataflow, BigQuery, Cloud Storage, Data Catalog, and time-travel. It also tests how to surface quality signals to dashboards and maintain lineage.

## Key Concepts

- Data quality framework per tenant (schema conformance, null checks, dedupe)
- Per-tenant isolation in BigQuery
- Data Catalog lineage and contract testing
- Rollback using BigQuery time travel and snapshots
- Testing strategy and drift monitoring

